{"subjectId":"javascript","id":"regex","title":"Regular Expressions","group":"Collections & Iteration","order":39,"html":"<p class=\"lead\">Patterns for searching, validating and transforming text. Write them as literals <code>/pattern/flags</code> or with <code>new RegExp(string, flags)</code>.</p>\n<section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-list\"></i>Syntax cheat sheet</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Token</th><th>Matches</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>.</code></td><td>Any char except newline (any char with the <code>s</code> flag)</td></tr><tr><td><code>\\d \\w \\s</code></td><td>Digit, word char <code>[A-Za-z0-9_]</code>, whitespace — uppercase negates</td></tr><tr><td><code>[abc]</code>, <code>[^abc]</code>, <code>[a-z]</code></td><td>Character class, negated class, range</td></tr><tr><td><code>^</code> <code>$</code> <code>\\b</code></td><td>Start, end (per line with <code>m</code>), word boundary</td></tr><tr><td><code>* + ? {n,m}</code></td><td>0+, 1+, 0–1, n to m — add <code>?</code> for lazy (<code>*?</code>)</td></tr><tr><td><code>(…)</code> <code>(?&lt;name&gt;…)</code> <code>(?:…)</code></td><td>Capture group, named group, non-capturing group</td></tr><tr><td><code>a|b</code></td><td>Alternation</td></tr><tr><td><code>(?=…)</code> <code>(?!…)</code> <code>(?&lt;=…)</code> <code>(?&lt;!…)</code></td><td>Lookahead, negative lookahead, lookbehind, negative lookbehind</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table><thead><tr><th>Flag</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>g</code></td><td>Global — all matches</td></tr><tr><td><code>i</code></td><td>Case-insensitive</td></tr><tr><td><code>m</code></td><td>Multiline <code>^</code>/<code>$</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>s</code></td><td><code>.</code> matches newlines (dotAll)</td></tr><tr><td><code>u</code> / <code>v</code></td><td>Unicode mode / Unicode sets (ES2024)</td></tr><tr><td><code>y</code></td><td>Sticky — match at <code>lastIndex</code> only</td></tr><tr><td><code>d</code></td><td>Record match indices</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-code\"></i>The main methods</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const text = \"Order #123 shipped on 2024-03-15, order #456 on 2024-04-01.\";\nconsole.log(/order/i.test(text));\nconsole.log(text.match(/#\\d+/));              // first match + details\nconsole.log(text.match(/#\\d+/g));             // all matches (no details)\nconsole.log(text.search(/\\d{4}/));\nconsole.log(text.replace(/(\\d{4})-(\\d{2})-(\\d{2})/g, \"$3/$2/$1\"));\nconsole.log(\"a1b22c333\".split(/\\d+/));</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>true\n[\n  '#123',\n  index: 6,\n  input: 'Order #123 shipped on 2024-03-15, order #456 on 2024-04-01.',\n  groups: undefined\n]\n[ '#123', '#456' ]\n22\nOrder #123 shipped on 15/03/2024, order #456 on 01/04/2024.\n[ 'a', 'b', 'c', '' ]</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-brackets-contain\"></i>Named groups and matchAll</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const log = \"user=asha id=7; user=ravi id=12\";\nconst re = /user=(?&lt;name&gt;\\w+) id=(?&lt;id&gt;\\d+)/g;\nfor (const m of log.matchAll(re)) {\n  console.log(m.groups.name, Number(m.groups.id), m.index);\n}\nconst { year, month } = \"2024-09\".match(/(?&lt;year&gt;\\d{4})-(?&lt;month&gt;\\d{2})/).groups;\nconsole.log(year, month);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>asha 7 0\nravi 12 16\n2024 09</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-eye\"></i>Greedy vs lazy, lookarounds</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const html = \"&lt;b&gt;bold&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;i&gt;italic&lt;/i&gt;\";\nconsole.log(html.match(/&lt;.+&gt;/)[0]);       // greedy: as much as possible\nconsole.log(html.match(/&lt;.+?&gt;/)[0]);      // lazy: as little as possible\nconsole.log(\"1234567.89\".replace(/\\B(?=(\\d{3})+(?!\\d))/g, \",\"));\nconsole.log(\"price: $30, €40\".match(/(?&lt;=\\$)\\d+/)[0]);\nconst strong = /^(?=.*[A-Z])(?=.*\\d)(?=.*[^\\w\\s]).{8,}$/;\nconsole.log(strong.test(\"Passw0rd!\"), strong.test(\"password\"));</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>&lt;b&gt;bold&lt;/b&gt; and &lt;i&gt;italic&lt;/i&gt;\n&lt;b&gt;\n1,234,567.89\n30\ntrue false</code></pre></figure>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-alert-triangle\"></i>The <code>lastIndex</code> trap</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const re = /a/g;\nconsole.log(re.test(\"a\"), re.test(\"a\"), re.test(\"a\"));</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>true false true</code></pre></figure>\n<div class=\"callout callout--warn\"><div class=\"callout-label\">Watch out</div><p>A regex with <code>g</code> or <code>y</code> is <strong>stateful</strong>: <code>test</code>/<code>exec</code> continue from <code>lastIndex</code>. Reusing one global regex across calls gives alternating results. Drop the <code>g</code> for <code>test</code>, or reset <code>re.lastIndex = 0</code>.</p></div>\n</section><section class=\"block\"><h3><i class=\"ti ti-variable\"></i>Dynamic patterns</h3>\n<figure data-lang=\"js\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>JavaScript</figcaption><pre><code>const escapeRegExp = (s) =&gt; s.replace(/[.*+?^${}()|[\\]\\\\]/g, \"\\\\$&amp;\");\nconst term = \"a.b\";\nconsole.log(new RegExp(term).test(\"axb\"), new RegExp(escapeRegExp(term)).test(\"axb\"));\nconsole.log(new RegExp(`^${escapeRegExp(\"1+1\")}$`).source);</code></pre></figure><figure data-lang=\"text\" class=\"code\"><figcaption>Output</figcaption><pre><code>true false\n^1\\+1$</code></pre></figure>\n<details class=\"qa\"><summary>What does the g flag change?</summary><div><p>With <code>g</code>, <code>match</code> returns all matches (without groups), <code>replace</code> replaces every match, <code>matchAll</code> requires it, and <code>test</code>/<code>exec</code> become stateful via <code>lastIndex</code>. Without it, only the first match is considered.</p></div></details></section>"}